{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vja6wAT2xwUv4jjavKGCZD","type":"tool_result","content":"    raise TypeError(\"Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\")\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\nFAIL: test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores (tests.test_publish.PublishTest.test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores)\nOK","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6972ebfb-7a70-445b-b42e-6a506673d6d8","uuid":"3bce752d-a209-4fa1-a3b6-8ccb956747d7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:12:45.919Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    raise TypeError(\"Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\")\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\nFAIL: test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores (tests.test_publish.PublishTest.test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores)\nOK","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Vja6wAT2xwUv4jjavKGCZD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1cXroTqZNH2AEacXfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012a9p4rBvWBUqHz8HvTupsi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-CXOfvp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with its three most similar existing stories,\n`similar: [{slug, score}]`. The score comes from `similarity()`, which returned\n`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`. That is a Python **`float`**.\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer refuses floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n- **First publish:** the table is empty, so `similar == []` and the item holds\n  no float (`published_at` is an `int`). It gets stored with a 201\n  (`similar=0` in the log).\n- **Every publish after that:** there is at least one existing story, so\n  `similar` holds a `{\"score\": <float>}`. `put_item` raises `TypeError`, and\n  `handler()` turns it into a 500. A score of zero is still `0.0`, a float, so\n  every publish fails once the library is non-empty, even with no overlap.\n\nThe existing test missed it because it publishes one story into an empty\ntable, which is the one case that never makes a score.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n1. **At the source:** `similarity()` now returns\n   `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`. Going through `str` gives an exact value like\n   `Decimal('0.4123')` instead of a long binary-float expansion.\n2. **At the storage boundary:** a new `to_dynamo()` recursively turns any\n   `float` into a `Decimal`. `publish()` runs it on the whole item just before\n   `put_item`. If a future field (or a client sending a number in `tags`) adds\n   a float, it can no longer cause a 500. This step is what stops the bug from\n   coming back.\n\n## Regression tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores` sends three publishes through\n  `handler()` against the boto3-faithful `FakeTable`. It checks that each one\n  returns 201 and that the stored scores are `Decimal`s with the right ranking.\n  Against the old `app.py` this test fails with the exact production\n  `TypeError`.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats` checks the converter on nested\n  dicts and lists.\n\nRun: `python3 -m unittest discover tests` (3 tests pass).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":371,"cache_read_input_tokens":25917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":371},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6972ebfb-7a70-445b-b42e-6a506673d6d8","uuid":"6a1ec2f9-4208-4a69-afe2-b2ac999fdee4","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:12:55.530Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1cXcQzSxZtdXVwsFXm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012a9p4rBvWBUqHz8HvTupsi":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-CXOfvp/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story with its three most similar existing stories,\n`similar: [{slug, score}]`. The score comes from `similarity()`, which returned\n`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`. That is a Python **`float`**.\nboto3's DynamoDB serializer refuses floats:\n\n```\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\n```\n\n- **First publish:** the table is empty, so `similar == []` and the item holds\n  no float (`published_at` is an `int`). It gets stored with a 201\n  (`similar=0` in the log).\n- **Every publish after that:** there is at least one existing story, so\n  `similar` holds a `{\"score\": <float>}`. `put_item` raises `TypeError`, and\n  `handler()` turns it into a 500. A score of zero is still `0.0`, a float, so\n  every publish fails once the library is non-empty, even with no overlap.\n\nThe existing test missed it because it publishes one story into an empty\ntable, which is the one case that never makes a score.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n1. **At the source:** `similarity()` now returns\n   `Decimal(str(round(..., 4)))`. Going through `str` gives an exact value like\n   `Decimal('0.4123')` instead of a long binary-float expansion.\n2. **At the storage boundary:** a new `to_dynamo()` recursively turns any\n   `float` into a `Decimal`. `publish()` runs it on the whole item just before\n   `put_item`. If a future field (or a client sending a number in `tags`) adds\n   a float, it can no longer cause a 500. This step is what stops the bug from\n   coming back.\n\n## Regression tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores` sends three publishes through\n  `handler()` against the boto3-faithful `FakeTable`. It checks that each one\n  returns 201 and that the stored scores are `Decimal`s with the right ranking.\n  Against the old `app.py` this test fails with the exact production\n  `TypeError`.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats` checks the converter on nested\n  dicts and lists.\n\nRun: `python3 -m unittest discover tests` (3 tests pass).\n"}}}
